course: dictionary
lesson: 8072
title: Relief: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word relief has more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one. Read the sentence and its clues. «After the test, she let out a long sigh of relief.» A sigh of relief shows that the worry is over, so relief here means a happy, calm feeling.
explain: «He took pain relief after he banged his knee.» The word pain is nearby, so relief must mean making the pain less. Ask yourself: what is relief doing in this sentence?
explain: «Relief teachers come in when the usual teacher is ill.» Here relief means someone who takes over another person's work for a while. The word teachers and the idea of taking over are the clues.
explain: Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you probably have the right one. If not, look at the clues again or check a dictionary.
fact: Relief is a noun. You can say relief (uncountable), or a relief when it means a person or thing that takes over work.
fact: Relief can mean the happy, calm feeling when something bad or worrying stops or doesn't happen, as in «what a relief».
fact: Relief can mean help such as food, money or shelter for people in trouble, as in «disaster relief» after floods.
fact: On a geography map, relief shows the ups and downs of the land: the hills and valleys.
fact: «Tax relief» means a tax cut, so people pay less tax.
exercise: «After the test, she let out a sigh of relief.» What does relief mean here? | A kind of map showing hills | A hard, heavy weight to carry | A test that is very hard | *A happy, calm feeling because a worry is over
exercise: «Relief aid arrived in the town after the floods.» What kind of relief is this? | *Help such as food and shelter for people in trouble | Pain medicine for a headache | A teacher who covers a class | Hills and valleys on a map
exercise: Lena says a relief map is just a flat drawing of a road. What is the correct meaning? | *A map showing the ups and downs of the land | A flat road with no hills | A map that tells you the time | A map of a shop with its prices
test: «He took pain relief after he banged his knee.» What does relief mean here? | Help for people after a flood | A teacher who covers a class | A happy feeling after a worry ends | *Making the pain less
test: «Relief teachers come in when the usual teacher is ill.» What does a relief teacher do? | Teaches the children to paint on a rock | *Takes over another teacher's work for a while | Gives out money to families | Makes the classroom darker
exam: Dev reads «Tax relief means a tax cut.» What does relief mean in this sentence? | Hills and valleys on a map | Help for people in trouble after a flood | *A reduction in the amount of tax people pay | A happy, calm feeling
